choice("Continue", B3-Ch03b-Desmond, v_current_scene = B3-Ch03b-Desmond)


ID: B3-Ch03b-Desmond
TEXT:

"Patrols rarely sweep this quarter, which makes it our standard entry point," Breynan says, beckoning us forward. "Stay close. I will show you how to draw down one of the green-eyed spheres in a matter of minutes."

"What was the accident the operator mentioned?" Kate asks, matching his stride. "When he said Desmond, did he mean the man stationed outside the quarantine ward?"

"The very same," Breynan says grimly. "The poor fellow went through an ordeal. He was pinned in a brutal skirmish and pleaded for an immediate extraction. It violated every safety protocol we have—the teleportation mechanism is centuries old and fails to lock onto turbulent auras. But the situation was desperate, so Barry pulled the lever. Desmond described the transit as having every muscle and tendon shredded apart simultaneously. The moment he materialized underground, he collapsed, vomiting blood and bile. He was bedridden for days. Even now, the memory rattles him so thoroughly that he requested a stationary guard post to avoid ever stepping onto the platform again."

"Grim," I mutter. "Did the damage linger, or did he make a full recovery?"

"He recovered physically within a week," Breynan says. "But we have never attempted an emergency extraction under duress since. The volatility is simply too extreme. Now, look up. Do you see that metal sphere hovering near the eaves? It will complete its aerial sweep shortly before descending to inspect the alleyway ahead. That is where we intercept it. Move quietly."

We slip into the adjacent alley with ease, unhindered by city sentries. After two minutes of circling above the rooflines, the sphere drops down as Breynan predicted, leveling out to hover at chest height.

"Hey!" Breynan calls out. "Metal sphere! I require an audience with the Overseer. Do you hear me?"

The metallic orb rotates, its single green lens focusing directly on Breynan. A brief hum resonates from its core before the flat, synthesized voice speaks.

"Request acknowledged," the drone intones. "Stand by. Initiating Overseer protocol."

choice(""Melindra, you're not sensing any of the royal guards nearby, right?"", B3-Ch03b-Royal, v_current_scene = B3-Ch03b-Royal)
choice(""Let's hope that we'll have more luck getting useful information out of it than Eiden."", B3-Ch03b-Useful, v_current_scene = B3-Ch03b-Useful)
choice(""Breynan, remember that we will have questions to ask too, so don't take too long."", B3-Ch03b-Questions, v_current_scene = B3-Ch03b-Questions)


ID: B3-Ch03b-Royal
TEXT:

"Melindra, you're not sensing any of the royal guards nearby, right?"

"None of the ones we ran into earlier," Melindra says, scanning the rooftops. "I cannot speak for the rest of their garrison, but there are no significant magical auras in our immediate vicinity. We should be clear."

"Overseer protocol initiated," the metal sphere announces, the dry synthesized tone shifting into a smoother, remarkably expressive cadence. "Greetings, Breynan. How may I be of assistance today?"

"You know why we are here, rust bucket," Breynan says. "You sent the invitation. Out with it."

"The Overseer protocol possesses no record of extending such an invitation," the Overseer replies smoothly. "Perhaps you are mistaken. If you specify the event to which you were invited, I will gladly direct you to the proper venue."

"Playing dumb," Melindra mutters.

"Or he is indicating we lack standing," Kate suggests, "and that he only speaks with official delegates recognized by the underground king."

"That is not the issue," Breynan tells us quietly. "He will yield the information once we find the right angle. Overseer! Have there been any recent alterations to the palace's security perimeter? The sort of vulnerability that might permit an undetected entry by rebel forces?"

"No such alterations have been implemented," the Overseer says. "Palace security remains at peak operational efficiency."

"What of conditions within the citadel?" Breynan asks. "Has the king of Ollendor shown symptoms of contracting an illness?"

"His majesty is in optimal health," the Overseer says. "Thank you for your concern."

"What about the newcomer in the king's retinue?" Kate asks. "How is Eiden interacting with the royal guard?"

A brief pause hangs in the air before the drone responds.

"The majority of the royal guard refuse to acknowledge Eiden as a legitimate authority and consider him an active threat," the Overseer says. "Eiden is cognizant of their sentiment and deliberately provokes them to observe their behavior."

"Sounds like him," Melindra says.

"Is there a way the resistance might exploit this friction between the guard and the Creator?" Breynan asks. "Does their conflict create an opening for an assault on the palace?"

"As previously stated," the Overseer intones, "no recent alterations have compromised palace security."

choice("Continue", B3-Ch03b-Vulnerability, v_current_scene = B3-Ch03b-Vulnerability)


